# performance-inefficient-vector-operation is intentionally disabled: its 27
# reserve() suggestions were mostly generator/test setup, including tiny component
# lists. The benefit does not justify spreading allocation tuning through that code.
# bugprone-exception-escape is disabled pending review: MSVC allocation and I/O
# paths dominate its findings, including CLI exceptions already caught by std::exception.
# Keep exception-policy changes separate from routine tidy fixes.
# Deferred after review; findings are saved for a separate follow-up:
# bugprone-integer-division: intentional integer grid coordinates (3 findings).
# bugprone-incorrect-roundings: sign-aware rounding matching FMath::SinCos (1).
# bugprone-return-const-ref-from-parameter: locally consumed projections (2).
# bugprone-signed-char-misuse: nonnegative int8_t avoidance indices (2).
# bugprone-suspicious-stringview-data-usage: Windows calls already pass lengths (5).
# bugprone-misplaced-widening-cast: mixes guarded/constant arithmetic with size
# calculations needing bounds review (17); defer that review rather than add casts.
# bugprone-narrowing-conversions: includes mission kill-count signedness policy (4).
# bugprone-unchecked-optional-access: 721 reports, including checked result wrappers
# and explicitly guarded optionals; too noisy for this rollout.
# Further deferred checks; preserve existing contracts and review findings separately.
# misc-misplaced-const: intentional const S7 pointer aliases (49 reports).
# clang-analyzer-cplusplus.Move: tests of defined moved-from container states (5).
# clang-analyzer-cplusplus.PlacementNew: SoA byte-array lifetime/zero-size storage needs review (14).
# misc-const-correctness: broad local-const style churn (268).
# modernize-avoid-c-arrays: array/API and fixture rewrites (68).
# modernize-return-braced-init-list: string count/character constructor overload concern (1).
# modernize-use-designated-initializers: widespread aggregate/math initializer churn (2832).
# modernize-use-emplace: mixed generator/test construction churn (61).
# modernize-use-equals-default: changes instrumented test-type triviality (1).
# modernize-use-integer-sign-comparison: mixed comparisons need range-contract review (37).
# modernize-use-std-numbers: includes constants deliberately matching FMath (5).
# cppcoreguidelines-avoid-do-while: statement macros and a directory-creation retry loop (7).
# cppcoreguidelines-avoid-non-const-global-variables: callback-observable test state (1).
# cppcoreguidelines-init-variables: output parameters and exhaustive branch assignments (15).
# cppcoreguidelines-macro-usage: test assertion macro preserving expression context (1).
# cppcoreguidelines-misleading-capture-default-by-value: this is already explicitly captured (2).
# cppcoreguidelines-missing-std-forward: callbacks deliberately invoked as lvalues (5).
# cppcoreguidelines-no-malloc: matching deallocation for S7-owned C API output (1).
# cppcoreguidelines-prefer-member-initializer: constructor sequencing needs separate review (2).
# cppcoreguidelines-pro-bounds-array-to-pointer-decay: C APIs and array fixtures (53).
# cppcoreguidelines-pro-type-member-init: scratch arrays populated before reading (12).
# cppcoreguidelines-pro-type-vararg: C APIs and bounded formatting calls (5).
# cppcoreguidelines-special-member-functions: mixed ownership/test-type policy changes (16).
# Deferred performance/readability findings; keep this rollout bounded:
# performance-enum-size: representation changes without demonstrated storage benefit (7).
# performance-inefficient-string-concatenation: widespread generator/diagnostic string rewrites (52).
# readability-avoid-nested-conditional-operator: mixed local expression/style rewrites (42).
# readability-convert-member-functions-to-static: test fixtures and subsystem method contracts (25).
# readability-implicit-bool-conversion: intentional flag/pointer truth tests; mixed style value (18).
# readability-make-member-function-const: includes logical mutations through shared SoA state (8).
# readability-math-missing-parentheses: broad precedence/style churn (243).
# readability-named-parameter: intentionally unused callback/test parameters (15).
# readability-qualified-auto: pointer spelling changes throughout tests and APIs (71).
# readability-redundant-member-init: conflicts with explicit initialization style (40).
# readability-simplify-boolean-expr: mixed literal cleanup and optional DeMorgan rewrites (6).
# readability-static-accessed-through-instance: tests using the uniform container instance API (4).
# readability-uppercase-literal-suffix: established lowercase f style; large mechanical churn (4850).
